  "problem": "Deterministic extraction lacked a measured acceptance boundary and a concrete residual queue. Successful results could be promoted without capture/parser receipts. Residual work could default to the entire corpus or ask a model to invent missing facts. Failed empirical thresholds could be silently flipped. Last-good public generation could be overwritten without publication validation.",
  "resulting_behavior": "reconcileEvidence requires a capture/parser receipt for every successful result and refuses promotion when evidence is missing. Partial dictionaries and stale observations are retained with reasons. createResidualTasks emits a bounded queue (not 3434 records) excluding credentials, forbidden access and unknown eligibility. Every residual has a public passage or an explicit insufficient-evidence outcome; LLM-from-memory is forbidden. publishDeterministicReadout reports attempt coverage, dictionary yield, working examples, unresolved essential fields and source differences with reproducible R03/R06 denominators of 3434. Failed R03/R04/R06 thresholds stay failed. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 and manifest 85b50522b4209d25dba70ad389d14d8b7e4a640384eb3d0d2a413e920aa67a2e remain unchanged. Publication is not authorized. Live fetch is forbidden. CLI stays fixture-only. Sealed accounting artifacts, normalization src and identity schema-catalog are unchanged. scripts/research/sweep.mjs is not invoked.",
